# PART B — HEAT OF FORMATION (ΔH°f)

## 1. What heat of formation is

[
\Delta H_f^\circ = \sum (\text{bond energies formed}) - \sum (\text{bond energies broken})
]

Exact value requires **quantum chemistry**.
We therefore use **Benson group additivity**, the **only accepted estimation method**.

---

## 2. Fragment the molecule (this is the key step)

### Structural groups present:

* 6 × **tertiary ring N (–N–)**
* 6 × **nitramine groups (–N–NO₂)**
* 4 × **bridgehead cage carbons**
* High **cage strain energy**

